      "content": "Those feelings of numbness and detachment are strong indicators that you are experiencing burnout. Your brain may be shutting down social engagement to protect you from emotional pain, which can make a new city feel cold and unwelcoming. While this protective mechanism is understandable, it does not mean you aren't real or that your presence doesn't matter to those around you—even just your passage through the city needs your connection to feel whole. Please consider speaking with a mental health professional who can help explore these deep feelings and offer personalized support.",
